-- title:
--   No cusp-free smooth-point chart at an end of the supersingular component
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ denotes its residue field. The finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is of those places $w$ which are rational (the structure map $\kappa\to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is onto), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` in the set `ssJSet q κ`; $s$ is an element of $W$. The inclusion `hle` records `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base-changed full level-$M'$ modular function field inside the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base-changed function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'`. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `integers` with a surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, with a scaling property for nonzero elements, together with a place map preserving degrees and compatible with divisors), and `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$.
--
--   The geometric data are: a field $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$; a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring `integers` of `fieldBar q M'` meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, with a surjective residue map to $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the reduction of $A$ on constants, and such that every nonzero element becomes a nonzero residue after multiplication by a constant); a finset $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$; and families $S_x$, $\varphi_x$, $\chi_{0x}$, $D_x$ assigning to every place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ a subring of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $A[T]\to S_x Q$, a ring homomorphism $S_x Q\to\kappa$ and a set of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are, by name: `h0`, that $F_{ss}$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$; `h1`, that $R$ lies over $s$, namely that for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has nonnegative order at every place at which the $j$-function (the image of `jq` in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`) has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image in $F_{ss}$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue; `h2`, that $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is invariant under the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` attached to a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hcard`, that $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements; `hpkg`, that for every place $Q\notin N$ the quadruple $(S_xQ,\varphi_xQ,\chi_{0x}Q,D_xQ)$ satisfies the fourteen clauses of a smooth-point package, which are literally the clauses listed in the conclusion below; `hdisj`, that for $Q,Q'\notin N$ a place lying in both $D_xQ$ and $D_xQ'$ forces $Q=Q'$; `hcusp`, that for $Q\notin N$ every $P\in D_xQ$ has $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j$ in `fieldBar q M'`; and `heqv`, that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut τ` preserves membership in $N$ and, for $Q\notin N$, carries $D_xQ$ to $D_x$ of the translated place, in the sense `smulDisc τ (Dx Q) = Dx (R.resAut τ hτ • Q)`.
--
--   The remaining hypothesis `hK` is a single existential statement providing the annuli at the ends of the component together with their node presentations; its clauses are grouped and summarised here, no clause being passed over. It asserts the existence of a family `An` of `Annulus A (fieldBar q M')` structures indexed by the places of $F_{ss}$ (each consisting of a domain of places, a parameter, a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, with the parametrisation, unique-point, $\mathrm{ord}$-of-parameter-difference and unit clauses of `Annulus`) such that: (i) for each $x\in N$ the parameter of `An x` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $x.\mathrm{ord}$ of its residue equal to $1$ and obeys a slope law expressing, for $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero residue and of order $0$ on the annulus, that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\cdot(P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\text{param})^{-x.\mathrm{ord}(R.\mathrm{residue}\,f)}$ is a unit of $A$ for every $P$ in the annulus; the modulus is nonzero; the annulus is disjoint from every disc $D_xQ$ with $Q\notin N$; and every place of the annulus satisfies the tube condition over $s$, namely $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of an $R_0$-integral $f$ as in `h1` is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to any $a\in A$ whose residue is $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$; (ii) annuli at distinct points of $N$ have disjoint domains; (iii) the domains are permuted, via `smulDisc`, by the level automorphisms preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, compatibly with the action of `R.resAut` on $N$; (iv) every rational place of `fieldBar q M'` satisfying the tube condition over $s$ lies in some disc $D_xQ$ with $Q\notin N$ or in the domain of `An x` for some $x\in N$; (v) for distinct $x,x'\in N$ there is $g\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero residue with $x.\mathrm{ord}$ of that residue nonzero, of order $0$ on the domain of `An x`, and a unit of $A$ at every place of the domain of `An x'`; and (vi) a further existential block of node presentations: fields $F_{Ix}$ over $\kappa$ with regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'` and places $b_x$ of $F_{Ix}$; an index type $\Lambda$ with subrings $C'l\subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which are discrete valuation rings with uniformisers $\varpi'l$ and a base index $l_0$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_cl$ with elements $\pi_Wl$ and exponents $El$, $E_0$; sets $S\,nd$ of places of `fieldBar q M'`, subrings $\mathcal N\,nd$ and local noetherian subrings $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$, and elements $c_x,c_y,c_u$; subject to the global clauses (residue-zero criterion in $C'l$ via $\varpi'l$, $C'l_0\le C'l$, $\varpi'l_0\ne 0$, algebraicity of $A$ over $C'l_0$, irreducibility of $\pi_Wl$, $1\le El$, invariance of $\varpi'l_0$ under tame-trivial inertia, and $\varpi'l_0^{E_0}=v\pi^{w}$ for a unit $v$ of $A$ and some $w\ge1$) and, for every $nd\in N$, the local clauses: rationality of $b_x\,nd$, of $nd$ and of the places of $S\,nd$; the description of $\mathcal N\,nd$ as the elements integral for $R_x\,nd$, for $R$ and at all places of $S\,nd$, with $A$-integral values there; the crossing relation $c_x\,nd\cdot c_y\,nd=\varpi'l_0^{E_0}c_u\,nd$ together with the four residue and order normalisations of $c_x$ and $c_y$ with respect to $R_x\,nd$, $b_x\,nd$ and $nd$; invariance of $S\,nd$, $c_x\,nd$, $c_y\,nd$ under the arithmetic Galois action of the tame-trivial part of inertia; two generation statements for `fieldBar q M'` by the rings $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and by $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-combinations from $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l_0$; and, for each $l$, the chain $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l_0\le\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l\le\mathcal N\,nd$, the characterisation of $S\,nd$ by integrality and maximal-ideal conditions on $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$, the inclusion of $C'l$ in $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$, a non-unit approximation by constants, a $C'l$-linear independence clause, the existence of a subring $B_x$ generated over the constants $C'l$ by a finite set, containing $c_x,c_y,c_u$ and with $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ its localisation, membership of $c_x,c_y$ in $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ with $c_u$ a unit there, and the existence of $\sigma:W_cl\to$ the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ and of an isomorphism $\iota$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (πW l ^ E l)` sending $\sigma$ to constants and $\varpi'l$ to $\pi_Wl$, under which elements of $\mathcal N_0\,nd\,l$ with prescribed $b_x\,nd$-order $n$ (resp. $nd$-order $n$) are congruent to a unit times $V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by $\pi_Wl$ and $U$ (resp. a unit times $U^n$ modulo the ideal generated by $\pi_Wl$ and $V$); the Hasse datum on the curve's own invariant: `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` lies in `fieldBar q M'`, and there are $a_0\in A$ with $J-a_0\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $R$-residue $0$ and $\mathrm{residue}(a_0)^q=s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$, and a constant $c'$ with $c'(J-a_0)\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonzero residue such that for every $nd\in N$ one has $J-a_0\in(R_x\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue and $nd.\mathrm{ord}(R.\mathrm{residue}(c'(J-a_0)))=-(b_x\,nd).\mathrm{ord}$ of that residue; disjointness of $S\,nd$ for distinct $nd\in N$; the tube condition over $s$ at every place of $S\,nd$; a permutation of $N$ attached to each `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` compatible with the sets $S\,nd$ and with the rings $(R_x\,nd).\mathrm{integers}$; equivariance of $N$ and of $S$ under the group generated by the level automorphisms via `R.resAut` and `smulDisc`; the identification $S\,nd=(\mathtt{An}\,nd).\mathrm{dom}$ for $nd\in N$; the statement that images of $R_0$-integral functions are $R_x\,nd$-integral; and, for each $nd\in N$, a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to $F_{Ix}\,nd$ compatible with the residues of $R_0$ and $R_x\,nd$ and such that an element lies in the valuation subring of $s$ precisely when its image lies in that of $b_x\,nd$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts: for every $Q\in N$, every subring $S$ of `fieldBar q M'`, every ring homomorphism $\varphi:A[T]\to S$, every ring homomorphism $\chi_0:S\to\kappa$ and every set $D$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the following conjunction is false: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every element of $A$ lies in $S$; $\varphi$ is formally smooth; $\varphi$ is formally unramified; $\varphi(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for every $a\in A$; $\chi_0(\varphi(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ for every $a\in A$; $\chi_0(\varphi(X))=0$; for every $c\in A$ of residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S\to A$ with $\chi(\varphi(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A$, with $\mathrm{residue}(\chi f)=\chi_0 f$ for all $f\in S$, and with $\chi(\varphi(X))=c$; every $f\in S$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue of that element in $Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is the image of $\chi_0f$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; $\varphi(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R$-residue equals $1$; a place $P$ belongs to $D$ if and only if $P$ is rational, every $f\in S$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for every $f\in S$ one has $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f)<1$ exactly when $\chi_0f=0$; for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S\to A$ with $\chi(\varphi(C\,a))=a$ and $\mathrm{residue}(\chi f)=\chi_0f$ there is a unique $P\in D$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f=\chi f$ for all $f\in S$; for $P\in D$, an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f\cdot h=g$ for some $g,h\in S$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h\ne0$; every nonzero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f=0$ for all $P\in D$ satisfies $c\cdot f=u$ for some nonzero constant $c\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and some unit $u$ of $S$; every $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in the valuation subring of all $P\in D$ lies in $S$; and, finally, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $j$-function for every $P\in D$.
--
--   Thus none of the $q+1$ places of $N$ carries a smooth-point package whose residue disc is free of cusps, in the precise sense of the fourteen clauses together with the nonnegativity of the order of $j$.
--
--   The places of $N$ are the $q+1$ ends of the supersingular component attached to $s$ in the stable reduction of the full level $q^2M'$ modular curve, and the statement says that no end admits an étale coordinate chart with a cusp-free residue disc, so that the ends are genuine singular points of the reduction rather than smooth points. It is used in the assembly of the supersingular regular prolongation together with its smooth-point charts, node presentations, crossing units, Igusa datum and inertia equivariance.
